{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And they beat the officers of the children of Israel.</b> The officers were Israelites and had compassion on their brethren, so as not to press them. And when they would deliver the bricks to the taskmasters, who were Egyptians, and the count was short, they would flog them — for not having pressed the laborers. Therefore those officers merited to become a Sanhedrin, and to be drawn from the spirit that was upon Mosheh and placed upon them, as it says: ״Gather to Me seventy men of the elders of Israel…״ — from those whose good deed you knew that they did in Egypt — ״for they are the elders of the people and its officers״ (Numbers 11). (Shemot Rabbah)" "<b>And they beat the officers of the children of Israel whom Pharaoh's taskmasters had set</b> over them as officers, <b>saying: Why, etc.</b> Why <b>did they beat them?</b> Because they would say to them, <b>Why have you not completed your quota, both yesterday and today,</b> the fixed quota upon you, <b>to make brick</b> — as the day before yesterday, which is the day before yesterday; and that was when the straw was given to them." "<b>And they beat.</b> A passive form — they were beaten by the hands of others: the taskmasters beat them."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:50:40.862844759Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}